# SAINTOS @VERSION@ (Fedora Remix @FEDORA@, KDE Plasma)

Built @BUILT_AT@ from SAINT commit `@COMMIT@`.

`SAINTOS-x86_64.iso` · SHA-256 `@SHA256@`

SAINTOS is a Fedora Remix: Fedora Linux @FEDORA@ with KDE Plasma, built from Fedora's own image
descriptions with SAINT installed natively. It is **not an official Fedora product** and isn't
endorsed by the Fedora Project. Fedora is a trademark of Red Hat, Inc.

## What's in it

- Fedora's KDE Plasma desktop, live session and Anaconda installer, unchanged underneath (same
  kernel, packages, updates and Secure Boot chain as Fedora).
- **SAINT** in `/opt/saint` with its own Python 3.12 environment. Menu: *SAINT*. Command: `saint`.
  The user service is off until you turn it on (`systemctl --user enable --now saint`, or the
  Control Center).
- **SAINTOS Control Center** (`saintos-control`): service, AI provider/model (detects Ollama),
  voice, permissions, capabilities, data folders, diagnostics, updates. It opens once on first login.
- SAINTOS look: dark Breeze with SAINT orange, the Halo wallpaper, SAINTOS boot splash.
- `saintos-diagnose`: read-only diagnostics folder.

## Not included / known limitations

- No AI model and no Ollama: install Ollama and pull a model you choose. SAINT's commands work
  without one; chat and planning need one.
- SAINT's speech models (~500 MB) download the first time SAINT starts.
- Window control uses KWin scripting. Keyboard/mouse automation (ydotool) isn't set up by
  default. Reading other apps' notifications isn't possible on Linux.
- Hosted-provider API keys are still stored in SAINT's config file (Secret Service planned).
- Updates: Fedora packages update with dnf/Discover. SAINT in `/opt/saint` updates by installing
  a newer SAINTOS build. Rebranded files (`/etc/os-release`) may revert to Fedora's after a
  `fedora-release` package update.
- Tested in VirtualBox only. Not tested on physical hardware.

See `docs/SAINTOS_RELEASE_STATUS.md` and `docs/DUAL_BOOT_INSTALLATION.md` in the source.
